    [BugFix] Fix CPP profiling dummy prefill routing with PCP (#18622)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    CPP startup profiling calls the model runner dummy path with one
    synthetic request. With PCP enabled, the generic V2 dummy batch is
    initialized with decode-only attention state and the PCP dummy fast path
    bypasses `partition_batch()`. A large CPP profiling sample can therefore
    enter the PCP decode O-projection communication path without being
    partitioned, where its token rows exceed the decode buffer capacity.
    
    This PR:
    
    - carries an explicit CPP-profile marker through the V2 model runner and
    input batch;
    - builds CPP dummy inputs with fresh-prefill metadata and
    `PrefillNoCache` attention state;
    - sends CPP profiling dummy batches through PCP `partition_batch()`
    while preserving ordinary capture/runtime dummy behavior;
    - skips the speculative drafter only for CPP profiling, matching the
    existing V1 behavior; and
    - adds unit coverage for CPP dummy construction, state restoration, and
    PCP partitioning.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. CPP startup profiling now works with PCP-enabled V2 deployments
    instead of routing large profiling dummy batches through the decode-only
    PCP path. There is no CLI or configuration API change.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Unit tests:
    
    ```bash
    python -m pytest -q \
      tests/ut/worker/test_v2_dummy_padding.py \
      tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py \
      tests/ut/worker/test_model_runner_v2.py \
      tests/ut/worker/test_worker_v2.py
    ```
    
    Result: `240 passed, 14 warnings`.
    
    End-to-end validation used GLM-5.2 W4A8 with PP=2, TP=2, PCP=4, EP
    enabled, MTP=1, eager mode, and `max_num_batched_tokens=20480`:
    
    - CPP collected all 64 startup samples and reported `Profiling completed
    successfully`;
    - the service reached `/health` HTTP 200 without the previous
    decode-capacity `ValueError`;
    - AISBench warmup: 5/5 requests succeeded;
    - fixed-length prefill (65,536 input tokens, concurrency 2): 24/24
    succeeded; and
    - variable-length prefill (40,960-81,920 input tokens, concurrency 2):
    24/24 succeeded.
    
    A CPP-disabled run of the same service and three workloads also
    completed with zero failed requests, covering the non-CPP path.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
